        type: "p",
        text: "About 135kms from Leh, Lamayuru reveals striking geological formations that have earned the village the name ‘Moonland’. Hiking through its eroded hills is an experience in itself, especially at sunrise and sunset, when light and shadow wash the terrain in hues of gold and crimson. Then there’s Hunder, where silent sand dunes stretch out against towering mountains, and the two-humped Bactrian camel still wanders. Hunder’s remoteness is part of its magic, making it ideal for trekking, camping, and presenting a rare chance to stay with a local family, to experience life at its most unfiltered.",
        page: 21
