        type: "p",
        text: "Then there’s Mawphlang, a sacred grove that offers a glimpse into nature as it once was: untouched, unbroken, and deeply revered. Protected for centuries by Khasi tribal customs and believed to be guarded by forest spirits, Mawphlang carries a palpable stillness, a silence that, in the summer, feels almost sacred, held together by green light, cool air, and the restful sense of something enduring.",
        page: 22
