    category: "culture",
    date: "April 2026",
    excerpt: "Baisakhi, celebrated annually on 13th/14th of April, marks the harvest of rabi crops and the beginning of a new solar year. The festival holds both agricultural and cultural significance, symbolising prosperity, gratitude, and new beginnings.",
    heroImage: "/images/stories/baisakhi-from-fields-to-festivities.webp",
    heroImageAlt: "Dancers in bright turbans and costumes performing in a wheat field",
    heroImageSource: "Spice Route - April 2026, PDF page 33",
